D = {
"Otto's Irresistible Noodles|HFLOTT": "Boil pasta in salted water until just short of al dente and save 1 cup of the water. Brown butter with sage over medium heat for 3 to 4 minutes. Finish the pasta in the pan with some pasta water for 30 seconds to 1.5 minutes. On low heat, melt in the cheese in two batches over 30 to 90 seconds. Season and serve at once.",
"Otyugh Steak|HFLOTT": "Heat a cast-iron skillet 5 minutes, then sear salted mushroom clusters in oil, 5 minutes per side. Lower to medium, press them under a heavy pan and brown again, about 5 minutes per side. Add butter, garlic and thyme for 45 seconds, then soy sauce. Baste the mushrooms with the butter for about 1 minute. Plate with parsley.",
"Oysters and Wild Rice in Mushroom Soup|HFLOTT": "Simmer wild rice with bay leaf for 40 to 60 minutes, then strain and save the liquid. Brown mushrooms in butter for about 12 minutes. Soften leek, celery and thyme for 6 minutes. Combine all with half-and-half and rice liquid, simmer 12 minutes, rest 15 minutes. Add smoked oysters, warm 8 minutes, and serve with chives.",
"Pan-Fried Fungi with Garlic Butter|HFLOTT": "Cook mushrooms with salt over medium-high heat for about 14 minutes until browned. Melt butter and soften shallots for 2 minutes. Add garlic and thyme for 40 seconds, then brandy, scraping up the browned bits. Stir in pepper and parsley, then serve.",
"Pan-Fried Knucklehead Trout|HF": "Heat the oven to 250°F. Dredge rested trout fillets in seasoned flour and pan-fry in oil and butter, 2 to 3 minutes per side. Keep them warm in the oven. Brown the remaining butter with shallot for about 2 minutes, add lemon juice and salt, and pour over the fish. Top with parsley and lemon wedges.",
"Par-Salian's Tea|HF": "Peel lemon zest into strips and smash ginger slices. Put two zest strips and one ginger slice in each of four mugs. Pour in about 1¼ cups boiling water and steep about 4 minutes. Stir in honey to taste. Slap mint sprigs to release their scent and add one to each mug.",
"Pegasus|PAF": "Simmer ginger, sugar and water covered for 10 minutes, steep 30 minutes, and cool to make the syrup. Muddle peaches, mint and lemon juice. Add 1 ounce of syrup, bourbon and ice, and stir about 30 seconds. Strain over crushed ice in two highball glasses. Top with bitters and a mint sprig.",
"Pickled Vine Blight Salad|HFLOTT": "Blanch green beans 3 minutes, chill, and pack into jars with a hot brine, garlic, bay and cloves. Refrigerate at least 48 hours. Salt the cabbage for 1 to 4 hours, rinse and dry it. Soak shallots 15 minutes. Whisk a dressing with bean brine and oil, then toss everything with the beans and parsley.",
"Pieglass|PAF": "Cook pumpkin puree on low 3 minutes, add spice, sugar, water and vanilla, simmer 2 minutes, strain, and cool as syrup. Whip cream with confectioners' sugar to soft peaks. In each pint glass, pour 12 ounces of cider and add ½ cup ice cream. Top with whipped cream and 2 tablespoons of syrup.",
"Plate of Silver|HFFOTM": "Roast potatoes at 450°F for about 35 minutes and cool 10 minutes. Press each flat to about ¾ inch on an oiled sheet, spaced 2½ inches apart. Brush with oil and salt, then roast about 25 minutes more, turning the sheet halfway. Top each with an anchovy fillet and parsley.",
"Plate-of-Gold|HF": "Warm jam 3 to 5 minutes, then simmer with ketchup, vinegar, sugar, soy sauce and salt for 1 minute and cool as the sauce. Heat oil to 390°F. Mix chilled flours, salt and sparkling water into a lumpy batter. Fry battered pieces 5 to 6 minutes per batch, drain, and keep warm in a 200°F oven.",
"Poetess|PAF": "Boil water and sugar, add lavender, steep 5 minutes, strain, and mix in butterfly pea powder dissolved in hot water. Cool. Stir tequila, vermouth and ½ ounce of syrup over ice for about 30 seconds. Strain over a large ice cube in each glass. Add lemon juice, lavender and lemon peel.",
"Potato Leek Soup|HF": "Fry bacon about 13 minutes and set aside. Soften leeks, celery and thyme about 5 minutes. Add potatoes, broth and salt, and simmer 15 to 20 minutes until soft. Blend smooth. Stir in cream and simmer about 5 minutes. Season and top with crumbled bacon. It can be served cold.",
"Potion of Restoration|HF": "Muddle 11 blackberries with sugar and lemon juice until the sugar dissolves. Add gin and butterfly pea powder if using, then ice, and shake for 30 seconds. Strain over ice into two glasses. Add ½ ounce crème de mure to each. Add a lemon twist and two blackberries.",
"Pumpkin Honey Beer Bread|HFLOTT": "Rub together a sugar, flour and butter topping and chill. Cook pumpkin 10 to 12 minutes until thick, add spices, and cool 15 minutes. Whisk the wet and dry batter parts, fold together, and pour into a 9 by 5-inch pan. Add topping. Bake at 350°F for about 45 minutes. Cool 20 minutes, then unmold.",
"Purple Grapemash No. 3|HFFOTM": "Chill two glasses. Blend rum, lime juice, grape jelly and ice cubes until slushy and smooth. Divide between the glasses. Garnish each with a lime slice and serve with straws.",
"Purskul Welcome Soup|HFLOTT": "Cook bacon about 14 minutes and keep 1½ tablespoons of fat. Soften onion, carrots, celery and herbs about 8 minutes. Cook tomato paste 2 minutes, then garlic and paprika 40 seconds. Add broth and simmer 10 minutes. Blend half the beans with 2 cups of the liquid, return all with the rest of the beans, and simmer 10 minutes. Add parsley and bacon.",
"Qualinesti Vegetable Stew|HF": "Heat the oven to 375°F. Warm garlic and thyme in oil 1 to 2 minutes and set aside. Cook onion 4 minutes, garlic 1 minute, then tomato puree about 7 minutes. Spread in the skillet with basil. Shingle sliced vegetables on top and drizzle with the garlic oil. Bake covered 30 minutes and uncovered about 20 minutes. Rest 10 minutes.",
"Quij's Plate|HFFOTM": "Brown sausage 3 to 4 minutes and set aside. Cook potatoes with water covered for 12 to 14 minutes. Add onions and pepper for about 8 minutes, then sage and garlic for 40 seconds. Stir in half-and-half and cook flat 8 to 10 minutes until browned. Return the sausage, make wells, and cook eggs covered 6 to 9 minutes.",
"Quith-pa|HF": "Grate orange zest and squeeze juice. Process apricots, ¼ cup coconut, zest, juice, vanilla and salt until finely chopped. Roll into 15 or 16 balls of about 1 inch and coat in the remaining coconut. Rest the balls 45 minutes. They keep about 3 days in an airtight container.",
"Ray of Frost|HFFOTM": "Chill two glasses. Stir gin, absinthe and vermouth over ice for about 30 seconds. Strain into the glasses. Run a lemon twist around each rim and drop it in.",
"Red Larch Crumblecakes|HFLOTT": "Dry the chickpeas, then microwave them about 6 minutes and cool. Heat the oven to 350°F. Mix flours, spices and salt, then add scallions, carrot, turkey and chickpeas. Fold in a beaten egg, yogurt and oil mixture. Bake in a loaf pan 55 to 60 minutes, brushing with butter halfway. Cool 20 minutes.",
"Reghed Venison Pot Roast|HF": "Tie and season the beef, then brown it on all four sides, about 13 minutes. Cook onion, paprika, flour and tomato paste, then deglaze with wine and add broth, apricots, garlic and thyme. Braise covered at 300°F for 1¾ hours. Add carrots, potatoes and apricot halves and cook 2¼ to 2¾ hours more until the beef reaches 200°F. Make gravy and slice.",
"Restoration|PAF": "In a large pitcher, stir coconut water, coconut milk, lemon juice and honey until the honey dissolves. Add lemon slices. Fill halfway with ice and serve in highball glasses at once.",
"Rewards|PAF": "Roll puff pastry to ⅛ inch and cut six circles of about 5½ inches. Press them into a muffin tin. Fill with a rhubarb and strawberry mix using ¼ cup each. Brush edges with egg wash and freeze 30 minutes. Bake at 400°F for 25 minutes until golden and bubbling. Cool on a rack.",
"Rime Of The Frostmaiden|PAF": "Freeze a bottle of wine in a pan for 6 hours. Scrape it into a blender with blueberries, blue curaçao, lemon juice and agave syrup, and blend smooth. Freeze 30 minutes to thicken. Pulse to loosen, pour into coupes, and serve at once.",
"River Fish Fry|HFLOTT": "Salt and pepper the fillets and rest them 10 minutes. Dredge in a seasoned cornmeal mix. Fry in shimmering oil over medium heat, 3 to 4 minutes per side, until the thick ends reach about 135°F. Rest on paper towels for 3 minutes and serve with lemon wedges.",
"Roast Gammon Pie|HFLOTT": "Line a pie plate with one pastry round and chill both rounds 30 minutes. Heat the oven to 450°F. Brown pearl onions 3 minutes. Cook leek and spices, then flour 1½ minutes, add broth and half-and-half, then sweet potato 8 minutes. Add brandy, mustard, ham and onions. Fill, top, vent, and bake 20 minutes, then at 375°F for 15 minutes. Cool 40 minutes.",
"Roasted Plums and Burrata|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 325°F. Toss plums with oil and brown sugar and caramelize cut-side down 3 to 4 minutes. Flip, add shallot, thyme and seasoning, and roast 4 to 5 minutes. Cool. Cut open burrata and drizzle with honey and oil. Arrange plums around it with parsley and fennel.",
"Rollrum|HF": "Muddle sugar and water until syrupy, then gently muddle in mint. Add ice and absinthe and shake 30 seconds. Divide over ice in two glasses and add seltzer if using. Slap mint sprigs to release their scent and use as garnish.",
"Root Vegetables, Gratin-Style|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 450°F. Rub a dish with garlic, rest 2 to 3 minutes, and butter it. Toss potatoes, turnips and beets separately with butter, thyme, salt, garlic and Parmesan. Stand the slices tightly in the dish with shallots and oil. Bake covered 45 minutes. Add the remaining Parmesan and bake 25 to 30 minutes. Rest 10 minutes.",
"Rothé Steak|HFFOTM": "Season steaks and rest them 1 hour. Heat a cast-iron skillet 7 minutes, add oil, and sear, flipping every 30 seconds, for 3 to 4 minutes. Add butter, garlic and thyme and baste while flipping. Cook to 120° to 125°F in about 7 minutes for medium-rare, or 130°F in 8 to 9 minutes for medium. Rest 10 minutes and slice.",
"Ruby Cordial|HFFOTM": "Shake port, brandy, lemon juice and grenadine with ice for about 30 seconds. Strain over ice into two glasses. Run a lemon twist around each rim, drop it in, and add a cherry.",
"Rumtack|PAF": "Heat the oven to 350°F. Warm butter and ginger beer 3 to 5 minutes, then stir in cocoa, sugar, spices, rum, vanilla, buttermilk and eggs. Mix with the dry ingredients and bake in a Bundt pan 50 to 60 minutes. Simmer a butter, sugar and rum glaze 5 minutes. Poke holes in the cake and soak with glaze in stages, 30 minutes each. Unmold and brush with the rest.",
"Saerloonian Glowfire|HFFOTM": "Place a sugar cube in each of two flutes. Add ½ ounce port and ½ ounce Poire Williams to each and swirl. Slowly add 3 ounces Prosecco to each. Garnish with a pear slice and serve immediately.",
"Salbread|HFFOTM": "Heat the oven to 350°F. Rub lemon zest into sugar, then whisk in yogurt, eggs, vanilla and oil. Fold in the flour, baking powder and salt mix just until combined. Bake in an 8-inch square pan about 40 minutes. Cool 40 minutes, unmold, and cut into squares.",
"Sarth|HFLOTT": "Marinate lamb in onion-garlic juice with oil and spices, and beef in pomegranate molasses with spices, each 6 to 24 hours. Thread meat and onion on double skewers. Grill over a medium-hot fire, turning every 3 minutes, for 10 to 12 minutes until medium-rare. Rest about 3 minutes and top with parsley or chives.",
"Scrap And Oil|PAF": "Stir together a yogurt and herb dipping sauce and chill it. Mix chickpea flour, rice flour and baking powder. Combine egg, squeezed vegetables, garlic, herbs and spices, then work in flour mix until patties hold. Fry ⅓-inch fritters in ⅛ inch of oil, 2 to 3 minutes per side. Drain and serve with the sauce.",
"Scrimshaw|PAF": "Shake rum, Licor 43, lime juice, coconut cream and chocolate bitters with ice for about 30 seconds. Double strain into two coupes and serve at once.",
"Seafoam|PAF": "Boil water and salt, add nori, and steep 30 minutes to 1 hour. Strain. Keep for up to 1 month in the refrigerator. Fill two highballs three-quarters with ice and divide tequila, lime juice and sparkling water. Add ¼ teaspoon of the saline to each, stir, and garnish with nori.",
"Seared Boar and Potatoes|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 375°F. Tie and season the pork, then brown it about 12 minutes. Reduce chicken stock by half in 3 to 4 minutes. Roast the pork on potatoes and onions until it reaches 140°F, about 60 minutes, then rest 10 to 15 minutes. Roast the vegetables at 450°F for 15 minutes. Slice the pork and serve with the stock.",
"Seelie Court Cheese and Potato Soup|HFFOTM": "Soften onion, celery and bay in butter about 7 minutes. Add garlic and thyme for 40 seconds. Add broth and potatoes and simmer covered about 25 minutes. Add cheese for 2 minutes and blend smooth. Stir in half-and-half and warm about 4 minutes. Add parsley and chives.",
"Sembian Honey-Glazed Rothé Ribs|HF": "Heat the oven to 325°F. Cook a ketchup, honey, mustard and spice sauce with onion for about 5 minutes. Season ribs, brush with sauce, and roast bone-side down 2½ to 3 hours until about 205°F. Raise the heat to 425°F, brush with the rest of the sauce, and roast 8 to 10 minutes. Top with scallions.",
"Sensate Palate Cleanser|HFFOTM": "Soften leek in butter about 7½ minutes in total. Blend peeled cucumber, leek and chicken broth in three batches, adding half-and-half to the last. Stir in lemon juice and salt, then diced cucumber. Chill about 4 hours. Stir, season, and serve with pepper and chives.",
"Shadowdark|PAF": "Pulverize 2 cherries in the bottom of each of two pint glasses. Divide the lager and cider between them. Top each with 1 ounce of cherry juice and serve at once.",
"Silverfruit Pie|HFFOTM": "Heat the oven to 350°F. Press a graham crumb crust into a 9-inch plate and bake about 12 minutes. Cool. Chill dried lychee halves at least 1 hour. Blend mascarpone, sugar, rosewater and vanilla, spread in the crust, and chill at least 1 hour. Top with lychees, brush with warm apple jelly, chill 30 minutes, and add lemon zest.",
"Skyway Special|HFLOTT": "Whip egg whites with sugar to stiff peaks and fold into a yolk, milk and flour batter. Cook tall mounds of batter in covered skillets over medium-low heat with a little water for steam. Cook 2 minutes, add a third scoop, then 4 to 6 minutes. Flip and cook about 4 minutes. Dust with sugar and serve.",
"Smoked Sausages and Kraut with Dwarven Mustard|HF": "Cook onion in oil about 15 minutes until caramelized. Add apple, sugar, sauerkraut, water and seasoning, and cook covered 25 to 35 minutes. Warm pierced sausages in simmering beer 5 to 10 minutes. Stir mustard into sour cream. Serve sausages on kraut with the mustard mix on the side.",
"Solamnic Mushroom Ragout with Dumplings|HFLOTT": "Brown pearl onions 3 minutes, then brown mushrooms in two batches, 8 to 10 minutes each. Cook leeks, carrot and bay 2 minutes, tomato paste 2 minutes, then garlic, paprika and flour 2 minutes. Add wine, simmer 3 minutes, add broth and carrots for 10 minutes, then leeks, onions and mushrooms for 5 minutes. Drop in dumpling dough and cook covered about 15 minutes.",
"Solstice Soup|HFLOTT": "Soften onion, celery, carrots and herbs about 13 minutes in total. Stir in flour for 1 minute, then broth. Add oats and leeks and simmer covered about 15 minutes. Off heat, add chicken, cream and seasoning and rest 30 minutes. Reheat without boiling, then add parsley.",
"Sooka|HFLOTT": "Simmer blueberries, sugar and water about 13 minutes, cool 40 minutes, and strain as syrup. Shake lemon juice, gin and butterfly pea for 30 seconds. Pour 1¼ ounces of syrup into each glass with ice. Strain the gin over a spoon to layer it. Add glittery seltzer, a lemon slice and blueberries.",
"Sornstag|HFFOTM": "Toast breadcrumbs 3 minutes and fry garlic and almonds in oil, 1 minute each. Brown seasoned venison in batches, about 4 minutes each. Cook onions 6 minutes, then spices 40 seconds, then wine and chicken broth. Simmer covered about 2 hours. Stir in cocoa, then a blended crumb, almond and parsley paste. Cook 15 to 25 minutes more. Top with almonds and parsley.",
"Sour Cream-Walnut Cake|HFFOTM": "Pulse a flour, sugar, cinnamon and walnut topping with butter and chill 20 minutes. Heat the oven to 350°F. Grind walnuts with flour, then mix with dry ingredients. Whisk eggs, sour cream, oil, vanilla and sugars, and fold in the flour mix. Top with crumbs in an 8-inch pan. Bake 40 to 45 minutes and cool.",
"Spiced Plum and Hazelnut Financiers|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 400°F. Brown butter 3 to 4 minutes and cool. Whisk sugar, hazelnut and all-purpose flours, and salt. Whisk in egg whites, brandy and the browned butter. Fill 12 muffin cups. Top each with a plum slice in spiced sugar. Bake about 25 minutes, rotating halfway. Cool 5 minutes in the tin.",
"Spiced Pork and Orange Peppers|HFFOTM": "Heat the oven to 425°F. Rub pork with oil and a spice mix, then brown on four sides, about 6 minutes in all. Cook onion and peppers about 8 minutes, then garlic and thyme 1 minute. Roast the pork over them until 140°F, 12 to 17 minutes. Rest to 145° to 150°F. Add vinegar and parsley to the vegetables and slice the pork over them.",
"Sprucebark Quaff|HFFOTM": "In a large pitcher, combine mint, cucumber and water. Refrigerate 2 hours to infuse before serving.",
"Squid Ink Pasta with Scallops|HFLOTT": "Cook pasta just short of al dente and save 1 cup of water. Sear salted scallops about 2 minutes, add 1 tablespoon butter, and set aside. Cook shallots, garlic and pepper flakes 2 minutes, then reduce wine by half in 4 to 6 minutes. Finish the pasta in the pan 30 to 90 seconds. Return scallops with lemon juice, butter and parsley.",
"Steak of the Deep|HFFOTM": "Soften onion and bay in oil about 3 minutes, then garlic and paprika 1 minute. Simmer sherry 1 minute. Add tomatoes and cook about 3 minutes. Nestle seasoned swordfish in the sauce, cover on low, and cook about 25 minutes to 130°F, turning halfway. Rest 5 minutes. Finish the sauce with parsley and more sherry, then spoon over the fish.",
"Stuffed Egg-Battered Toast|HF": "Mix mascarpone, walnuts and vanilla. Cut a 2-inch pocket in each brioche slice and fill with about 1 tablespoon. Soak in egg, milk and salt, then cook in butter 2 to 3 minutes per side. Warm maple syrup on low for a few minutes. Dust the toast with confectioners' sugar and drizzle with syrup.",
"Stuffed Gourd with Gruyère and Spinach|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 400°F. Wring out spinach. Cook onion 3 minutes, garlic 40 seconds, then toast quinoa 4 minutes. Add broth, simmer covered about 15 minutes, then add cream cheese for 10 minutes. Stir in cheeses and spinach. Bake squash halves cut-side down 20 to 24 minutes. Fill, top with cheese and butter, and bake at 475°F for 8 to 10 minutes.",
"Stuffed Trout|HFFOTM": "Heat the oven to 450°F. Season the trout cavities. Toast breadcrumbs in butter about 6 minutes. Cook shallot and pepper about 3½ minutes, then garlic and lemon zest 40 seconds. Mix with the crumbs, lemon juice and parsley. Stuff each trout with about ⅓ cup. Bake about 12 minutes to 140°F. Rest 5 minutes and serve with lemon.",
"Surrogate Steaks|HF": "Heat the oven to 200°F. Mix meat with soy sauce, garlic powder, thyme and salt, and shape two steaks of 5 inches by 1¼ inches. Press one side in pepper. Sear unpeppered side about 4 minutes and the peppered side 2 minutes, then keep warm. Make a brandy, broth and cream sauce in about 10 minutes with mustard, lemon and chives.",
"Sweet Apple Tart with Celestial Caramel Drizzle|HFLOTT": "Cook sugar to deep amber, about 16 minutes, then add spices, butter, cream and vanilla. Cool at least 1½ hours. Roll pastry to 12 inches, fan apples on it, fold the border, and chill 30 minutes. Bake at 400°F for 32 to 35 minutes. Brush with warm jelly, cool, drizzle with caramel, and serve.",
"Sweet Butter Ale|HFLOTT": "Simmer ale, ginger, cloves and nutmeg, then 5 minutes more. Whisk yolks and brown sugar, temper with 1½ cups of the ale, and return all to the pot. Heat gently 6 to 10 minutes without boiling until as thick as whole milk. Whisk in butter and heat about 5 minutes. Serve in warmed mugs with nutmeg.",
"Sword Coast Seafood Bouillabaisse|HF": "Soften onion about 4 minutes. Add leek, garlic, fennel seed, pepper flakes and saffron for 1 minute, then tomato paste and wine. Add fish stock, tomatoes and orange zest and simmer about 20 minutes. Add anise liqueur and clams, covered, for 5 minutes. Add fish and mussels and cook 8 to 14 minutes. Rest 5 minutes and serve with garlic toasts.",
"Talyth|HFFOTM": "Process flour, cheese and seasonings, cut in butter, then add milk to form a dough. Roll two logs, wrap, and chill at least 2 hours. Heat the oven to 350°F. Slice into thirty ¼-inch rounds and press a sausage slice on each. Bake 24 to 28 minutes, swapping sheets halfway. Press the sausage again and cool.",
"Tamarind Balls|HFFOTM": "Pick seeds from tamarind pulp. Process it with dates, sugar, vanilla and salt for 30 seconds to 1 minute. Roll 2-teaspoon portions into eighteen balls of about 1 inch. Coat in large-crystal sugar. Store airtight at room temperature up to 4 days.",
"Tarnsar|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 450°F. Toss sweet potatoes and onions in oil and roast 8 minutes. Add pork tenderloin brushed with a hoisin, five-spice and garlic mix. Roast 18 to 20 minutes until 135°F to 138°F. Rest until 145°F to 150°F, 5 to 10 minutes. Slice and serve over the vegetables with scallions.",
"Tarsis-Style Shrimp|HFFOTM": "Poach shrimp in water with lemon juice, dill stems, salt and peppercorns for 10 to 15 minutes until the liquid reaches 170°F. Chill in ice water, dry, and halve lengthwise. Whisk a mayonnaise, yogurt, dill and lemon dressing. Fold in shrimp and celery, and chill about 2 hours. Add scallion greens and serve.",
"Tavern \"Steak\"|HF": "Make a dill-yogurt sauce and an olive and fig sauce from softened figs and chopped olives, capers, garlic and oil. Cook onion 4 minutes and garlic 1 minute, then mix with ground lamb and beef. Form four 6-ounce patties. Grill about 4 minutes, flip, and grill 3 minutes for 125° to 130°F. Rest 3 minutes and serve with the sauces.",
"Tavern Crickets|HFFOTM": "Heat the oven to 300°F. Whisk chile-lime seasoning, garlic powder, cayenne, salt and pepper. Toss peanuts, pepitas and crickets with melted butter, then the spices. Bake on a lined sheet about 20 minutes, stirring three times. Cool. Store airtight up to 1 week.",
"Tavern Noodles|HFFOTM": "Cook onions in 3 tablespoons oil about 30 minutes. Add rosemary and garlic for 40 seconds, then wine, reducing by half in about 2½ minutes. Boil fettuccine until just short of al dente and save 1 cup of water. Toss the pasta with the onions 1 minute. Off heat, add oil, garlic, Parmesan and pasta water. Add parsley and chopped egg.",
"Tavern Punch|PAF": "In a large pitcher or punch bowl, muddle strawberries until fully broken down. Add lager, ginger beer, blood orange juice and lemon juice. Stir gently and serve at once.",
"Tearoom Cookies|PAF": "Sift flour, matcha and salt. Beat butter soft, then beat in confectioners' sugar 1 to 2 minutes, then the egg yolk, then the flour mix. Shape a log of 1 to 1½ inches by 12 inches and chill at least 2 hours. Heat the oven to 350°F. Slice ⅓ inch thick, top with pistachios, and bake 11 to 13 minutes. Cool 5 minutes on the sheet.",
"Tears of Selûne|HFFOTM": "Simmer mirin, sake, soy sauce, sugar and paprika about 5½ minutes until foamy, then cool 5 to 6 minutes into a glaze. Skewer cubed fish, oil it, and grill over medium-high heat for 6 to 8 minutes, turning halfway. Brush with glaze at the end. Serve over rice with scallions and sesame seeds.",
"The Bag|PAF": "Stir amaretto, pistachio liqueur, coffee liqueur, espresso and heavy cream with ice for 30 seconds. Strain over ice into two rocks glasses and serve at once.",
"The Bored Weasel's Salty Fish Surprise|HFLOTT": "Soak salt cod 24 to 48 hours with at least four water changes. Simmer about 15 minutes until flaky. Cook sliced potatoes 3 minutes in the cod water. Slowly cook onions with bay 25 to 30 minutes, then garlic 1 minute. Layer potatoes, onions, cod, eggs, olives and oil in a dish. Bake covered at 375°F for 40 minutes, then uncovered at 450°F for 10 to 15 minutes.",
"The Hoard|PAF": "Salt and drain tomatoes 30 minutes, then mix pico de gallo and chill. Melt cheese, cornstarch and evaporated milk on low about 5 minutes with seasonings for the sauce. Heat the oven to 375°F. Build two layers of chips, sauce, beans, jalapeños and cheese. Bake 5 minutes. Top with pico, cotija, avocado mix, sour cream, radish and cilantro.",
"The Mindflayer|HF": "Blend ginger, sugar and lime juice about 1 minute, strain, and keep about ½ cup of syrup. Return it to the blender with grape juice concentrate, vodka and ice and blend until smooth. Divide between two tall glasses, garnish with grapes if using, and serve at once.",
"Thrakel-Seared Beef in Red Sauce|HFFOTM": "Marinate sliced flank steak in rice wine, soy sauce, cornstarch and sugar for 15 to 30 minutes. Mix a sauce of broth, vinegar, sesame oil, ketchup and seasoning. Sear the beef in two batches, about 2 minutes each. Brown tomatoes 3 minutes. Cook onion and scallion greens about 3 minutes, then the ginger-garlic mix 45 seconds. Add sauce 45 seconds, then the beef and tomatoes for 1 minute.",
"Tika's Honey Mead|HFFOTM": "Chill two coupes. Shake mead, orange juice, gin, honey syrup and lemon juice with ice for about 30 seconds. Strain into the glasses. Run an orange twist around each rim and drop it in.",
"TPK (Total Party Katastrophe)|PAF": "Boil lemongrass in water, whisk in sugar, tamarind and vanilla, and let sit 30 minutes. Strain and cool the base. In a pitcher, stir 1 cup of base with passion fruit juice, vodka, Aperol, lime juice, kiwi and pomegranate arils. Pour over ice into six rocks glasses and serve at once.",
"Traveler's Stew|HF": "Toss beef in seasoned flour and brown in batches, about 5 minutes each. Deglaze with beer, then add broth and paprika. Simmer covered on low 1½ to 2 hours until tender. Add onion, carrots and potatoes and simmer about 30 minutes. Stir in parsley, season, and serve hot.",
"Trencher Bread|HFFOTM": "Mix whole-wheat and all-purpose flours, cornmeal, salt and leaveners. Add milk and oil, knead smooth, and divide into four balls. Rest 15 minutes. Roll each to 11 inches and cook in a skillet over medium heat, 3 to 4 minutes per side. Keep the rounds warm in a 125°F oven and serve immediately.",
"Trolltide Candied Apples|HF": "Spear apples on sticks and set them on parchment. Boil sugar, corn syrup, coloring and water, then simmer 15 to 18 minutes to 300° to 310°F, adding vanilla near the end. Dip and twirl each apple, drain the excess, and return to the parchment. Cool and set 20 minutes.",
"Trolltide Punch|HFLOTT": "Heat the oven to 350°F. Core apples, fill with brown sugar and water, and bake covered 25 to 40 minutes. Simmer hard cider, Madeira, brandy, spices, lemon and clove-studded orange zest about 10 minutes. Add the apples and simmer 10 minutes more. Serve in warmed mugs with a twist of orange zest.",
"Twice-Baked Cockatrice Wings|HF": "Heat the oven to 300°F. Toss wings with baking powder, salt and pepper and set them skin-side up on a rack. Roast 40 minutes. Raise to 425°F and roast about 40 minutes until crisp. Sprinkle with garam masala and roast 10 minutes more. Serve hot.",
"Two Hares Inn Rabbit Stew|HFFOTM": "Brown seasoned chicken thighs about 10 minutes each batch, then remove the skin. Cook mushrooms 7 to 10 minutes, then onions about 4 minutes. Add garlic, herbs and flour for 1 minute, then wine. Add tomatoes, broth and chicken, and simmer covered 35 to 45 minutes. Rest the liquid 5 minutes, skim, reduce about 4 minutes, and add parsley.",
"Tymora's Coins|PAF": "Boil water and sugar, add lavender, steep 5 minutes, strain, and cool as syrup. In a pitcher, combine lemon juice, lemon slices, all the syrup and ouzo. Add ice and stir for 30 seconds. Add club soda. Serve over ice with lavender sprigs.",
"Underdark Lotus with Fire Lichen Spread|HF": "Heat the oven to 425°F. Roast chickpeas and carrots with cumin, cayenne, oil and salt for about 25 minutes. Blend with water, lemon juice, tahini and oil until smooth and creamy, adding water by the tablespoon as needed. Drizzle with oil and serve with radishes, cucumber or romaine.",
"Undermountain Alurlyath|HFFOTM": "Process cucumber to a pulp and wring it in a towel for juice. Shake sherry, honey syrup and lemon juice for about 10 seconds. Stir in 1 cup of cucumber juice. Divide over ice in two glasses and top each with 3 ounces of seltzer. Garnish with a cucumber slice.",
"Utmost Discretion|PAF": "In each of two flutes, stir 1 teaspoon sugar, 3 dashes of bitters and 1 ounce of sherry until the sugar dissolves. Add 4 ounces of sparkling wine to each and stir gently. Garnish with a cookie and serve at once.",
"Vada's Vanilla Buns|HFFOTM": "Toast coconut about 4 minutes, cool, and pulse. Cook a flour and water paste, cool it about 8 minutes, and mix with milk, egg, flour and yeast. Rest 15 minutes. Knead in sugar, salt, butter, vanilla seeds and coconut. Let rise about 1 hour. Shape 12 buns and rise about 1 hour. Bake at 375°F for 20 to 24 minutes. Cool 15 minutes.",
"Vedbread|HF": "Cook chopped mushrooms and shallots in butter 11 to 14 minutes, add thyme and Parmesan, and cool. Heat the oven to 425°F. Mix a flour, Gruyère and buttermilk dough and roll to 12 by 18 inches. Spread the filling, roll tight, and cut into 1¼-inch pieces. Brush with egg and bake about 18 minutes. Cool 5 minutes.",
"Wedding Soup|HFLOTT": "Simmer anchovies, broth and Parmesan rinds covered about 1 hour, then discard the rinds. Mix bread soaked in half-and-half with sausage, beef, cheese, herbs and egg, and roll ¾-inch meatballs. Cook them about 5 minutes in boiling water until they float. Soften onion, carrots and celery about 8 minutes, add garlic, and combine with broth. Cook couscous and escarole about 8 minutes.",
"Whole Roast Boar|HFFOTM": "Score the fat and rub with brown sugar, salt and pepper. Chill 12 to 24 hours. Roast at 325°F for about 5 hours until 190°F near the bone. Rest 30 minutes. Optionally crisp at 475°F for 8 to 10 minutes and rest 15 minutes. Make a port sauce with shallots, tomato paste, port, broth and jam, then butter and vinegar.",
"Wild Strawberry Salad|HFLOTT": "Whisk vinegar, shallot, orange zest and salt and rest about 10 minutes. Whisk in honey and oil. Save 1½ tablespoons. Toss lettuce with the dressing, seasoning, most of the mint and strawberries. Top with the rest of the mint and strawberries and the saved dressing.",
"Wood Elf Forest Salad|HF": "Whisk orange and lemon zest, lemon juice, vinegar, honey and salt, add shallot, and rest 10 minutes. Whisk in oil. Toss brussels sprouts with the dressing and rest about 30 minutes. Add radicchio, chives and quartered orange slices. Sprinkle with edible flowers if using.",
"Wren Pot Pie|HFLOTT": "Soften shallots about 6 minutes. Cook parsnips with water covered about 15 minutes until the liquid is gone. Cook onion and pepper 5 minutes, flour 1½ minutes, then broth, half-and-half and vermouth. Add parsnips, shallots, chicken and peas. Bake 12 minutes at 400°F. Top with a buttermilk batter and bake at 450°F for 18 to 20 minutes. Cool 10 minutes.",
"Yawning Portal Buttermilk Biscuits|HF": "Heat the oven to 450°F and grease an 8-inch pan. Cut chilled butter into the dry mix until pea-size, then stir in buttermilk. Pat the dough into the pan and score into nine squares. Bake about 30 minutes, rotating halfway. Cool 5 minutes, brush with butter, and cool about 12 minutes more.",
"Yuan-Ti Ceremonial Soup|HFLOTT": "Soak bread in water about 10 minutes. Blend it in two batches with almonds, garlic and a stream of oil until smooth. Blend in sherry, vinegar and salt. Chill at least 4 hours. Stir, season, and serve with olive oil, thin grape slices and reserved almonds.",
"Zzar|HF": "Whip cream and sugar until just thickened, add ½ ounce amaretto, and chill. Shake the remaining 3 ounces of amaretto, coffee liqueur and milk with ice for 30 seconds. Divide over two ice cubes in each of two glasses. Float the whipped cream on top and serve at once.",
}
